// =====================================================================
// Scene: "Drifting in the Void"
// Style: Generative Ambient / Evolving Drone
// =====================================================================

#BPM=50
#QUANTIZE=auto

// Slowly cycle through modes every 8 macro-cycles (bars) to create an 
// endless feeling of floating through different emotional states.
#SCALE_SEQ={ (0, 8): D3 dorian | (8, 16): F3 lydian | (16, 24): A3 dorian | (24, 32): C3 major}

// --- AUTOMATION ---
// Sending slow, independent LFOs to CC11 (Expression) and CC74 (Filter Cutoff).
// Because they have different float speeds, they will organically drift in 
// and out of phase with each other over time.
let ambient_motion = (
  cc11@sine(40, 100, 0.0625) | 
  cc74@tri(20, 90, 0.03125)
)

// --- T1: Lush Evolving Pads ---
// A wide 9th chord spanning 8 full cycles. Because we are using the scale 
// sequence above, playing the root (0) automatically morphs the chord to fit 
// the current mode perfectly.
T1(octave: 0, span: 8) with .vel(75) .gate(100):
  ( [ 0+2+4+6+8 _ _ _ ] | ambient_motion )

// --- T2: Sub / Grounding Drone ---
// A deep, unwavering root note.
T2(octave: -2, span: 8) with .vel(85) .gate(100):
  [ 0 _ _ _ ]

// --- T3: Shimmering Generative Arps ---
// This uses a `diverge` arp pattern playing at 1/8th normal speed (.speed(0.125)).
// Heavy humanization (up to 250ms of timing jitter) gives it a loose, 
// wind-chime-like quality that ignores the rigid MIDI grid.
T3(octave: 2, span: 4) with .arp(diverge) .speed(0.125) .vel(55) .humanize(25, 250.0):
  [ 0+2+4+6 ]
  [ 2+4+6+8 ]

// --- T4: Granular / Delay Plucks ---
// A Euclidean rhythm (3 hits across 8 steps) feeding a heavy "stut" (delay) modifier.
// The `?60` applies a 60% probability, meaning these textural notes will 
// only occasionally strike, letting the delay tails bleed out into the silence.
T4(octave: 3) with .vel(70) .stut(6, 0.7, 0.25) .E(3, 8) .humanize(10, 50.0):
  [ 4 6 7 9 ] ?60
